title: Anything reads anything
intro: Components name what they know as outputs. A Text, a Counter, a Bar or a wire shows any of them, a counter does something when it reaches a value, and flags work outside dialogue.
project: Platformer | Outputs

chapter: A speedometer with no code | A Text's Output
select: Player
look: -6, -2, 5
create: Text
rename: Speedometer
set: Transform.Position.Y = 1
set: Text.Size = 0.4
set: Text.Value = {0:0.0} m/s
pick: Text.Output = Speed
expectvalue: Speedometer.Text.Output = Speed
explain: field:Text.Output | Output | Every component names what it knows as outputs: a body's speed and height, health, a board's score and moves, the dungeon floor, whose turn it is, the beat, a faction's gold. This list is what the player has.
say: With no Track, a text reads the entity it's inside, so this one shows the player's speed. Its Value says how: the zero in braces is the output.

chapter: Counting to a value | Reaches, and a wire from Reached
select: Score
set: Counter.Reaches = At Least
set: Counter.Reach = 1
set: Counter.Reach Message = FirstCoin
explain: field:Counter.Reaches | Reaches | A counter can do something as it reaches a value: send a message, and turn on its own output Reached.
select: Bridge
add: Wire
pick: Wire.From = Score
pick: Wire.Output = Reached
choose: Wire.Input:choice = Show
expectvalue: Bridge.Wire.Output = Reached
explain: field:Wire.Output | Output | A wire carries any output that gives a number or true or false. This one shows the bridge once the score reaches one coin.

chapter: Flags outside dialogue | A trigger sets one, the lever needs it
create: Empty
rename: Rules
add: Trigger
pick: Trigger.Message = FirstCoin
pick: Trigger.Do = Set Flag
set: Trigger.With = Rich
select: Lever
set: Switch.Needs Flag = Rich
expectvalue: Lever.Switch.NeedsFlag = Rich
explain: field:Switch.NeedsFlag | Needs Flag | Switches, doors, spawners and panels can need a flag now. Until a trigger, a dialogue or a script sets it, this lever won't budge.

chapter: Playing it | Run for the coin
play
hold: Right 3
waitfor: Bridge | 5
explain: game | The bridge | The first coin brought the score to one, so its Reached came on and the wire showed the bridge, and the trigger set the flag the lever needs. The speedometer read the player all the way.
stop
